<section class="hero compact">
    <p class="eyebrow">EMERALD / PACKAGE TOOLCHAIN</p>
    <h1>pkgrebuild</h1>

    <p class="lead">
        Rebuild and reinstall an already installed package, typically after a
        library or ABI change.
    </p>

    <div class="command-line"># pkgrebuild [options] &lt;package&gt;</div>

    <h2 id="help">
        <code>pkgrebuild help</code>
    </h2>

    <pre><code>Usage:
    pkgrebuild &lt;options&gt;

Options:
    (no args)        rebuild toolchain AND base (default)
    -t, --toolchain  rebuild toolchain only
    -b, --base       rebuild base only
    -h, --help       Show this help</code></pre>
</section>

<section class="doc">
    <h2 id="usage">Usage</h2>

    <pre><code>pkgrebuild --help
pkgrebuild &lt;package&gt;</code></pre>

    <p>
        The utility checks that the package exists, rebuilds from its associated
        port data, and reinstalls the result. Use it for controlled repair;
        ordinary upgrades should go through <code>emerald upgrade</code> or
        <code>emerald sysup</code>.
    </p>
</section>
